      "writtenOn": "2023-08-15T05:52:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Understood.\nThis is ok but I\u0027m thinking if we can do better by using forbidden capabilities instead of introducing these flags. \ne.g. Introduce DEFAULT_FORBIDDEN_CAPABILITIES \u003d [NET_CAPABILITY_LOCAL_NETWORK].\n\nThus, for previous use cases, the semantics will be:\n1. The caller only wants to see local networks.\n-\u003e NetworkRequest(NET_CAPABILITY_LOCAL_NETWORK)\n2. The caller only wants to see non-local networks. (Default behavior)\n-\u003e NetworkRequest(forbidden \u003d NET_CAPABILITY_LOCAL_NETWORK)\n3. The caller wants to see all networks.\n-\u003e NetworkRequest(forbidden \u003d [])\n\nIn that way the CS might have better control over these callbacks in the rematching process instead of blocking them just before notify callback.\nJust an idea but not sure if this even make senses.\nWDYT?",
      "parentUuid": "06e101e8_3537e667",
